---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import { site } from '../../site.config.mjs';
const social = [
  ['Podcast', 'https://essamcafe.com'],
  ['YouTube', site.social.youtube],
  ['Medium', site.social.medium],
  ['LinkedIn', site.social.linkedin],
  ['Twitter', site.social.twitter],
].filter(([, u]) => u);
---

<Layout title="About" description="Ahmed Essam. Staff engineer at Apple, former founder, host of قهوة عصام. Twenty years of making software work, in Arabic too.">
  <article class="about">
    <header class="top">
      <p class="eyebrow">About</p>
      <h1>I make software work. Then I make it work in Arabic.</h1>
      <p class="lead">
        Twenty-plus years of engineering, a company I founded, and a podcast with more than a hundred episodes.
        Today I'm a Staff engineer at Apple, building the tooling that lets AI agents do real work on real codebases.
      </p>
    </header>

    <section>
      <h2>Now</h2>
      <p>
        I was part of the team that brought Claude into Apple engineering. Before an approved tool existed, I adapted an
        open-source coding agent to Apple's policy and security requirements and got teams working with it. Since then I've
        built an internal framework that lets designers and program managers turn a prompt into a working prototype, and
        I spend a lot of my time on the unglamorous part of AI: evaluating what models actually produce.
      </p>
      <p>
        On my own time I train small language models at home, past the fifth version now. I study how a one-word change in
        a question changes a model's answer, and I build tools that turn a codebase into a graph so an agent can see side
        effects, hot spots and test coverage before it touches anything.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>Scale</h2>
      <p>
        At Apple I designed a distributed UI automation platform for international markets, covering many languages,
        devices and account states. It replaced the work of roughly three hundred manual QA contractors, I hired and
        onboarded the team that runs it, and it is still running. I also added framework-level right-to-left and
        mixed-direction text support used across the App Store, Music, Podcasts and TV, and built Arabic search for the
        App Store.
      </p>
      <p>
        Before that, at Facebook, I owned crash reporting in the mobile SDKs that ran at startup for hundreds of millions of
        iOS users, and built the tools that kept every team inside its binary size budget.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>Founder years</h2>
      <p>
        In 2011 I founded F16Apps in Flat6Labs' first cohort. We built an on-device personalization engine, a compressed
        knowledge graph plus a per-user graph, running entirely in memory on an iPhone 4 with no server round trip. It
        shipped first in Neatly, a Twitter client whose Smart Timeline learned what you cared about. About seventy thousand
        people used it across six platforms, and The Next Web, Adweek and Android Central wrote about it.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>Arabic, since 2007</h2>
      <p>
        I'm a native Arabic speaker and I've been fixing Arabic in software for most of my career. In 2008, before Android
        supported Arabic at all, I wrote and open-sourced the text-shaping core that shipped as Better Arabic Reshaper and
        was later ported to Python. I contributed right-to-left work to Quran Android, built Arabic support for Windows
        Mobile, and wrote a free Arabic book on ASP.NET. This site exists partly because no platform renders Arabic the way
        it deserves.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>قهوة عصام</h2>
      <p>
        Essam Cafe is my podcast. More than a hundred episodes, in Arabic, with people I might agree or disagree with.
        Series on taking an idea to an MVP, on soft skills for engineers, and long conversations with guests who build
        things. New episodes land on this site automatically.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section lang="ar" dir="rtl" class="ar">
      <h2>بالعربي</h2>
      <p>
        أنا أحمد. مهندس برمجيات منذ أكثر من عشرين سنة، أعمل في آبل، وأسّست شركة قبل ذلك، وأقدّم بودكاست قهوة عصام.
        أهتم بأن يعمل البرنامج كما يجب، وبأن تُكتب العربية فيه كما تستحق. هذا الموقع يجمع ما أنشره في مكان واحد.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>Elsewhere</h2>
      <ul class="social">
        {social.map(([label, url]) => <li><a href={url}>{label}</a></li>)}
      </ul>
    </section>
  </article>
</Layout>

<style>
  .about { max-width: 720px; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 40px; }
  .top { display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 16px; }
  h1 { font-size: 44px; line-height: 1.1; letter-spacing: -0.02em; }
  .lead { margin: 0; font-size: 22px; line-height: 1.5; color: var(--muted); }
  section { display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 12px; }
  h2 { font-size: 24px; }
  p { margin: 0; font-size: 19px; line-height: 1.6; }
  .ar h2 { font-size: 30px; }
  .ar p { font-size: 21px; line-height: 1.9; }
  .social { list-style: none; padding: 0; margin: 0; display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 8px; }
  .social a { display: inline-flex; align-items: center; min-height: 44px; padding: 0 16px; border: 1px solid var(--line); background: var(--card); border-radius: 999px; text-decoration: none; font-size: 16px; }
  @media (max-width: 560px) { h1 { font-size: 32px; } .lead { font-size: 19px; } p { font-size: 18px; } }
</style>
